This is the model for the throttle cable adapter, it can be either folded, or 3d printed if you have access to suitable plastics.

(engine bays are hot places! PLA and PETG will go soft!)

This mount uses the the VW Transporter van throttle pedel sensor thing, which has an arm that is attached to the vans accelerator pedal.

The part number of the item you need to get from the VW transporter is 7H2721503E - you can get these on ebay for £20-30 roughly.

Inside this unit, there are 2 return springs, it is very easy to open this item via the screws and clips - remove the inner (smaller spring) as the pedal will be too stiff if both springs are used.

A good shackle for attaching the Toyota MR2 cable to the lever arm you will find on ebay described as "Honda Yamaha Kawasaki Suzuki Trumpet nipple Clevis Quick Release cable end New" "A (1) NEW ZINK PLATED TRUMPET NIPPLE CLEVIS QUICK RELEASE CABLE END WILL FIT MANY BIKES - 31MM LONG - 8MM INSIDE WIDTH - 13MM WIDE - 6MM CLEVIS HOLE - SO WILL FIT MANY BIKES"

